From 6f05f2ad4127413a2b027dab486818f94f07f04d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:24:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 1099 redfin: brightness trace (kern.sweet_bl_trace) and
 cold-boot fix (kern.sweet_bl_fix)

After every cold boot CoreBrightness sets the backlight to 1 (of 1023) and
ignores the slider; after a backboardd restart it works.

kern.sweet_bl_trace (default 3, boot-arg sweetbltrace): "SWEET BLT:" lines,
rate-limited (20/s, bursts of 60): bit 0 user-space property reads/writes of
AppleARMBacklight and AppleCLCD with the process, bit 1 every IOMFB
user-client call except the swap path. The "backlight brightness" line is
rate-limited instead of 8 a boot.

kern.sweet_bl_fix (default 7, boot-arg sweetblfix):
 1 with AppleARMBacklight, IOMFBBrightnessLevel is CoreBrightness's
   brightness factor (0..1.0 in 16.16), not nits: stored, no DCS (it put
   DBV 0x4/0x6 over the backlight level at every display on/off);
 2 AppleCLCD starts with IOMFBBrightnessLevel 1.0, not 250 nits;
 4 the ALS sends a neutral 100 lux sample at its client's ReportInterval
   until sensd's first sample (CoreBrightness starts with samples flowing,
   as after a backboardd restart).
